// kadane's Algorithm
Sliding Window (Understandable Explanation)
🧠 Core idea (simple words)

Instead of checking all possible subarrays (slow ❌),
we expand and shrink a window while keeping track of the best answer (fast ✅).

Think of it like this:
You keep a window of numbers
You keep adding numbers to the window (expand)
If the window becomes bad (sum < 0), you throw it away
You always remember the best sum seen so far

Why this works for Maximum Subarray
👉 If your current sum becomes negative, it will only reduce any future sum.

So:
“A negative prefix is useless — discard it.”

This idea = Kadane’s Algorithm
(It’s technically a special form of sliding window)


const arr=[-2,1,-3,4,-1,2,1,-5,4];
